 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-verilog"><span>module muxN_w_beh
  #( parameter N = 8, W = 16 )
  (
    input  wire [$clog2(N)-1:0] sel,
    input  wire [N*W-1:0]       din_flat, // flattened: {D_{N-1},...,D_0}
    output wire [W-1:0]         dout
  );
  // extract
  wire [W-1:0] D [0:N-1];
  genvar i;
  generate
    for (i = 0; i &lt; N; i = i + 1) begin : UNPACK
      assign D[i] = din_flat[(i+1)*W-1 -: W];
    end
  endgenerate

  assign dout = D[sel];

endmodule
</span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="5527" data-end="5588">This relies on the synthesizer to implement the physical mux.</p>
<hr data-start="5590" data-end="5593">
<h2 data-start="5595" data-end="5634">6 — Complexity, delay, and tradeoffs</h2>
<p data-start="5636" data-end="5673"><strong data-start="5636" data-end="5673">Gate count (2:1 building blocks):</strong></p>
<ul data-start="5674" data-end="5846">
<li data-start="5674" data-end="5795">
<p data-start="5676" data-end="5795">Single-bit <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>:</mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!:\!1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>: uses <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> 2:1 muxes. Each 2:1 mux = 2 AND + 1 NOT + 1 OR (or optimized AOI implementations).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5796" data-end="5846">
<p data-start="5798" data-end="5846">Multi-bit width <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span></span></span></span>: multiply counts by <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5848" data-end="5878"><strong data-start="5848" data-end="5878">Delay (tree of 2:1 muxes):</strong></p>
<ul data-start="5879" data-end="6042">
<li data-start="5879" data-end="5931">
<p data-start="5881" data-end="5931">Each 2:1 mux contributes one level of logic delay.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5932" data-end="5990">
<p data-start="5934" data-end="5990">For <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2^k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, tree depth = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k = \log_2 N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9386em; vertical-align: -0.2441em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.207em;"><span style="top: -2.4559em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2441em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> 2:1 stages.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5991" data-end="6042">
<p data-start="5993" data-end="6042">Overall propagation delay ≈ <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k \times t_{2:1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7651em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span><span class="mrel mtight">:</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6044" data-end="6076"><strong data-start="6044" data-end="6076">Decoder + AND + OR approach:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="6077" data-end="6231">
<li data-start="6077" data-end="6121">
<p data-start="6079" data-end="6121">Decoder delay + AND delay + OR tree delay.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6122" data-end="6231">
<p data-start="6124" data-end="6231">One-hot method can have faster selection (decoder can be fast) but OR tree of width <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> may be expensive.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6233" data-end="6275"><strong data-start="6233" data-end="6275">Transmission gates / pass transistors:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="6276" data-end="6416">
<li data-start="6276" data-end="6344">
<p data-start="6278" data-end="6344">Low logical depth (often one pass), very fast and compact in CMOS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6345" data-end="6416">
<p data-start="6347" data-end="6416">Must manage on-resistance, voltage drop, and buffering at the output.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6418" data-end="6436"><strong data-start="6418" data-end="6436">Tri-state bus:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="6437" data-end="6569">
<li data-start="6437" data-end="6511">
<p data-start="6439" data-end="6511">Very simple wiring for shared bus. Useful when many masters share a bus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6512" data-end="6569">
<p data-start="6514" data-end="6569">Requires one-hot enables produced by a decoder/arbiter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6571" data-end="6590"><strong data-start="6571" data-end="6590">Power and area:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="6591" data-end="6760">
<li data-start="6591" data-end="6648">
<p data-start="6593" data-end="6648">Replicating wide muxes consumes area linearly in width.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6649" data-end="6760">
<p data-start="6651" data-end="6760">For very wide buses, prefer wide 2:1 blocks rather than many single-bit instantiations for layout efficiency.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6762" data-end="6765">
<h2 data-start="6767" data-end="6810">7 — Concrete example: 8-to-1, 16-bit mux</h2>
<ul data-start="6811" data-end="7160">
<li data-start="6811" data-end="6853">
<p data-start="6813" data-end="6853">Inputs: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>…</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_0 \dots D_7</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">7</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, each 16 bits.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6854" data-end="6882">
<p data-start="6856" data-end="6882">Select: 3 bits <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S[2:0]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6883" data-end="7160">
<p data-start="6885" data-end="6908">Implementation options:</p>
<ul data-start="6911" data-end="7160">
<li data-start="6911" data-end="7038">
<p data-start="6913" data-end="7038">Hierarchical tree of 2:1 16-bit muxes: need <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">7</span></span></span></span> 16-bit 2:1 mux blocks; total single-bit 2:1 blocks = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>112</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16 \times 7 = 112</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">16</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">7</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">112</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7041" data-end="7160">
<p data-start="7043" data-end="7160">Decoder + AND + OR: 3-to-8 decoder + 8 × (16-bit AND) + 16-input OR (per bit) — area comparable but different layout.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7162" data-end="7165">
<h2 data-start="7167" data-end="7188">8 — Practical tips</h2>
<ul data-start="7189" data-end="7688">
<li data-start="7189" data-end="7291">
<p data-start="7191" data-end="7291">For RTL, prefer <code data-start="7207" data-end="7227">out = inputs[sel];</code> style and let synthesis tool choose optimal mux implementation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7292" data-end="7412">
<p data-start="7294" data-end="7412">For ASIC custom layouts, use transmission gates for the final stage if you need very low delay and can control layout.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7413" data-end="7542">
<p data-start="7415" data-end="7542">For FPGAs, the synthesizer maps muxes to LUTs — depth and LUT usage matter: build with tree structure or let the tool optimize.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7543" data-end="7688">
<p data-start="7545" data-end="7688">Ensure select signals are glitch-free / stable before enabling outputs when using tri-state or pass-transistor methods to avoid bus contention.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7690" data-end="7693">
<p data-start="7695" data-end="7714">If you want, I can:</p>
<ul data-start="7715" data-end="7986">
<li data-start="7715" data-end="7816">
<p data-start="7717" data-end="7816">Provide a polished LaTeX page with the definitions and the Verilog examples in theorem/lemma style.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7817" data-end="7896">
<p data-start="7819" data-end="7896">Show an explicit gate-level netlist for a 4:1 4-bit mux built from 2:1 gates.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7897" data-end="7986">
<p data-start="7899" data-end="7986">Provide transistor-level CMOS transmission-gate schematics (textual description only).</p>
</li>
</ul>
