<p data-start="52" data-end="214">A <strong data-start="54" data-end="75">multiplexor (mux)</strong> is a digital component that selects one of many input signals and forwards it to a single output line based on control (select) signals.</p>
<ul data-start="216" data-end="368">
<li data-start="216" data-end="273">
<p data-start="218" data-end="273"><strong data-start="218" data-end="229">Inputs:</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> data lines (or buses if multi-bit).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="274" data-end="307">
<p data-start="276" data-end="307"><strong data-start="276" data-end="288">Outputs:</strong> 1 line (or 1 bus).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="308" data-end="368">
<p data-start="310" data-end="368"><strong data-start="310" data-end="327">Select lines:</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_2 N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9386em; vertical-align: -0.2441em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.207em;"><span style="top: -2.4559em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2441em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> bits (to pick one input).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="370" data-end="488">A <strong data-start="372" data-end="389">multi-bit mux</strong> works the same way but handles entire data <strong data-start="433" data-end="451">words or buses</strong> instead of single bits. For example:</p>
<ul data-start="489" data-end="550">
<li data-start="489" data-end="550">
<p data-start="491" data-end="550">A 4:1 mux for 8-bit buses chooses between four 8-bit words.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="552" data-end="555">
<h3 data-start="557" data-end="581"><strong data-start="561" data-end="581">How to Build One</strong></h3>
<ol data-start="582" data-end="1090">
<li data-start="582" data-end="772">
<p data-start="585" data-end="711"><strong data-start="585" data-end="632">Start from 2:1 muxes (basic building block)</strong>:<br data-start="633" data-end="636">
A 2:1 mux picks between two inputs using one select bit.<br data-start="695" data-end="698">
Formula:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="true">‾</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y = (\overline{S} \cdot D_0) + (S \cdot D_1).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">Y</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1333em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord overline"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8833em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.8033em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="overline-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="774" data-end="942">
<p data-start="777" data-end="827"><strong data-start="777" data-end="824">Combine in a tree to handle multiple inputs</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="831" data-end="942">
<li data-start="831" data-end="898">
<p data-start="833" data-end="898">For <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> inputs, arrange 2:1 muxes in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_2 N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9386em; vertical-align: -0.2441em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.207em;"><span style="top: -2.4559em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2441em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> levels.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="902" data-end="942">
<p data-start="904" data-end="942">Example: 8 inputs → 3 levels, 7 muxes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="944" data-end="1090">
<p data-start="947" data-end="987"><strong data-start="947" data-end="984">Scale to multiple bits (wide bus)</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="991" data-end="1090">
<li data-start="991" data-end="1039">
<p data-start="993" data-end="1039">Replicate the mux structure for each bit, OR</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1043" data-end="1090">
<p data-start="1045" data-end="1090">Use wide 2:1 mux blocks operating on vectors.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1092" data-end="1095">
<h3 data-start="1097" data-end="1134"><strong data-start="1101" data-end="1134">Common Implementation Methods</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1135" data-end="1379">
<li data-start="1135" data-end="1190">
<p data-start="1137" data-end="1190"><strong data-start="1137" data-end="1159">Tree of 2:1 muxes:</strong> Fast, modular, balanced delay.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1191" data-end="1273">
<p data-start="1193" data-end="1273"><strong data-start="1193" data-end="1216">Decoder + AND + OR:</strong> One-hot select signals drive gates; often used in ASICs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1274" data-end="1379">
<p data-start="1276" data-end="1379"><strong data-start="1276" data-end="1320">Transmission gates or tri-state buffers:</strong> Hardware-efficient for buses, common in low-level designs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1381" data-end="1384">
<h3 data-start="1386" data-end="1414"><strong data-start="1390" data-end="1414">Why is it important?</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1415" data-end="1563">
<li data-start="1415" data-end="1487">
<p data-start="1417" data-end="1487">Used in CPUs for register selection, ALU inputs, routing in datapaths.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1488" data-end="1563">
<p data-start="1490" data-end="1563">Essential for any system needing to choose between multiple data sources.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1565" data-end="1568">
<h2 data-start="1570" data-end="1606"><strong data-start="1573" data-end="1606">Plain Summary in One Sentence</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1607" data-end="1845">A multi-bit multiplexor is a digital switch that selects one of many multi-bit inputs and outputs it, using a few select lines to control which input is chosen; it is built by combining simple 2:1 muxes or using decoders and gating logic.</p>
