32L3.36437 12.4785C3.40893 12.2616 3.45789 12.0745 3.52453 11.8926L3.6173 11.6621C3.71685 11.4352 3.83766 11.2176 3.97765 11.0127L4.15343 10.7783C4.34386 10.5462 4.58164 10.312 4.90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="957f01cd-97e4-4f82-85d1-ef75cc3a86ef" data-testid="conversation-turn-14" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-sm:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="957f01cd-97e4-4f82-85d1-ef75cc3a86ef" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="317">You’re describing a <strong data-start="20" data-end="64">bottom-up hardware construction approach</strong> (common in courses like <em data-start="89" data-end="102">Nand2Tetris</em>), where <strong data-start="111" data-end="169">every digital component is built using only NAND gates</strong> as the universal primitive. Here’s a <strong data-start="207" data-end="317">clear overview and summary of what this means for building a multi-bit multiplexor and related components:</strong></p>
<hr data-start="319" data-end="322">
<h3 data-start="324" data-end="350"><strong data-start="328" data-end="350">High-Level Process</strong></h3>
<ol data-start="351" data-end="1380">
<li data-start="351" data-end="488">
<p data-start="354" data-end="402"><strong data-start="354" data-end="400">Start with NAND as the only primitive gate</strong></p>
<ul data-start="406" data-end="488">
<li data-start="406" data-end="488">
<p data-start="408" data-end="488">NAND is universal: you can implement any Boolean function from NAND gates alone.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="489" data-end="808">
<p data-start="492" data-end="522"><strong data-start="492" data-end="520">Build basic gates first:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="526" data-end="808">
<li data-start="526" data-end="584">
<p data-start="528" data-end="584"><strong data-start="528" data-end="535">NOT</strong> from NAND: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>NOT</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mtext>NAND</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{NOT}(x) = \text{NAND}(x,x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NOT</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NAND</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="588" data-end="660">
<p data-start="590" data-end="660"><strong data-start="590" data-end="597">AND</strong> from NAND: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>AND</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mtext>NOT</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>NAND</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AND}(a,b) = \text{NOT}(\text{NAND}(a,b))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">AND</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NOT</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NAND</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="664" data-end="763">
<p data-start="666" data-end="763"><strong data-start="666" data-end="672">OR</strong> from NAND (via De Morgan): <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>OR</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mtext>NAND</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>NOT</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>NOT</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{OR}(a,b) = \text{NAND}(\text{NOT}(a), \text{NOT}(b))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">OR</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NAND</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NOT</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">NOT</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="767" data-end="808">
<p data-start="769" data-end="808"><strong data-start="769" data-end="776">XOR</strong> from combinations of the above.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="809" data-end="1022">
<p data-start="812" data-end="856"><strong data-start="812" data-end="854">Use these to build more complex gates:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="860" data-end="1022">
<li data-start="860" data-end="1022">
<p data-start="862" data-end="886"><strong data-start="862" data-end="883">Multiplexor (MUX)</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="true">‾</mo></mover><mo>∧</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∨</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y = ( \overline{S} \land A ) \lor ( S \land B ).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">Y</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1333em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord overline"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8833em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.8033em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="overline-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∨</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="962" data-end="1022">Implement this using AND, OR, and NOT built from NAND gates.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1023" data-end="1227">
<p data-start="1026" data-end="1058"><strong data-start="1026" data-end="1056">Extend to multi-bit gates:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1062" data-end="1227">
<li data-start="1062" data-end="1158">
<p data-start="1064" data-end="1158">A multi-bit MUX (say 16-bit) is an <strong data-start="1099" data-end="1128">array of single-bit MUXes</strong> sharing the same select line.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1162" data-end="1227">
<p data-start="1164" data-end="1227">For <strong data-start="1168" data-end="1178">n bits</strong>, replicate the single-bit structure <strong data-start="1215" data-end="1226">n times</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1228" data-end="1380">
<p data-start="1231" data-end="1264"><strong data-start="1231" data-end="1262">Build multi-way components:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1268" data-end="1380">
<li data-start="1268" data-end="1344">
<p data-start="1270" data-end="1344">For an 8-way MUX, cascade multiple 2-way MUXes in a tree (fork structure).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1348" data-end="1380">
<p data-start="1350" data-end="1380">Select lines control the tree.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1382" data-end="1385">
<h3 data-start="1387" data-end="1429"><strong data-start="1391" data-end="1429">Summary of Implementation Strategy</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1430" data-end="1767">
<li data-start="1430" data-end="1466">
<p data-start="1432" data-end="1466"><strong data-start="1432" data-end="1446">Primitive:</strong> NAND (binary gate).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1467" data-end="1520">
<p data-start="1469" data-end="1520"><strong data-start="1469" data-end="1485">Basic gates:</strong> Build NOT, AND, OR, XOR from NAND.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1521" data-end="1616">
<p data-start="1523" data-end="1616"><strong data-start="1523" data-end="1541">Complex gates:</strong> Build MUX and DEMUX using AND/OR/NOT combinations (thus ultimately NANDs).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1617" data-end="1694">
<p data-start="1619" data-end="1694"><strong data-start="1619" data-end="1639">Multi-bit gates:</strong> Replicate single-bit versions for each bit in the bus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1695" data-end="1767">
<p data-start="1697" data-end="1767"><strong data-start="1697" data-end="1717">Multi-way gates:</strong> Combine 2-way gates hierarchically (forked tree).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1769" data-end="1772">
<h3 data-start="1774" data-end="1795"><strong data-start="1778" data-end="1795">Plain Summary</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1796" data-end="2064">Start with NAND gates only. Build NOT, AND, OR from NAND. Combine them to make a single-bit MUX. For multi-bit MUX, replicate the single-bit MUX across all bits with a shared select line. For multi-way MUX, arrange 2-way MUXes in a tree. Everything remains NAND-based.</p>
<hr data-start="2066" data-end="2069">
<p data-start="2071" data-end="2319" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to <strong data-start="2089" data-end="2199">write the explicit Boolean expressions and NAND-only formulas for all these gates (NOT, AND, OR, XOR, MUX)</strong>, and then <strong data-start="2210" data-end="2272">show how many NAND gates are needed for a 16-bit 4-way MUX</strong>? Or should I keep it at this conceptual level?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.6851