  if c then x else y.
</span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="1599" data-end="1668">This is the direct analog of a hardware mux but generalized to types.</p>
<hr data-start="1670" data-end="1673">
<h2 data-start="1675" data-end="1750"><strong data-start="1678" data-end="1750">3. How NAND-level universality parallels Type-Theoretic universality</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="1751" data-end="2018">
<li data-start="1751" data-end="1823">
<p data-start="1753" data-end="1823">In hardware, <strong data-start="1766" data-end="1774">NAND</strong> is universal: any Boolean function can be built.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1824" data-end="2018">
<p data-start="1826" data-end="2018">In Coq/Lean, <strong data-start="1839" data-end="1872">Π-types (dependent functions)</strong> and <strong data-start="1877" data-end="1906">Σ-types (dependent pairs)</strong> plus <strong data-start="1912" data-end="1931">inductive types</strong> are universal:<br data-start="1946" data-end="1949">
They can represent all logical connectives and all data structures.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2020" data-end="2028">Mapping:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_1rjym_13 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="2029" data-end="2340" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2029" data-end="2080"><tr data-start="2029" data-end="2080"><th data-start="2029" data-end="2047" data-col-size="sm">Classical Logic</th><th data-start="2047" data-end="2080" data-col-size="md">Type-Theoretic (Curry–Howard)</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2134" data-end="2340"><tr data-start="2134" data-end="2185"><td data-start="2134" data-end="2152" data-col-size="sm"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p \land q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.75em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span></td><td data-start="2152" data-end="2185" data-col-size="md"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A \times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></spa