.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="2342" data-end="2431">So, a Coq system is like building <strong data-start="2376" data-end="2430">combinational logic out of Π and Σ instead of NAND</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="2433" data-end="2436">
<h2 data-start="2438" data-end="2485"><strong data-start="2441" data-end="2485">4. Extending to Categorical Type Systems</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="2486" data-end="3112">
<li data-start="2486" data-end="2725">
<p data-start="2488" data-end="2589">Coq and Lean implement <strong data-start="2511" data-end="2536">dependent type theory</strong> formalized as <strong data-start="2551" data-end="2588">Cartesian closed categories (CCC)</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2592" data-end="2725">
<li data-start="2592" data-end="2611">
<p data-start="2594" data-end="2611">Objects = types</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2614" data-end="2648">
<p data-start="2616" data-end="2648">Morphisms = functions (proofs)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2651" data-end="2725">
<p data-start="2653" data-end="2725">Products = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>∧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5556em;"></span><span class="mord">∧</span></span></span></span>, coproducts = <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>∨</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lor</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5556em;"></span><span class="mord">∨</span></span></span></span>, exponentials = implication.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2726" data-end="2818">
<p data-start="2728" data-end="2818">Adding <strong data-start="2735" data-end="2754">dependent types</strong> → fibrations → higher categories → homotopy type theory (HoTT).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2819" data-end="2943">
<p data-start="2821" data-end="2843">The generalization is:</p>
<ul data-start="2846" data-end="2943">
<li data-start="2846" data-end="2943">
<p data-start="2848" data-end="2943"><strong data-start="2848" data-end="2943">Boolean gates → Logical connectives → Type constructors → Functors/Natural transformations.</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2944" data-end="3112">
<p data-start="2946" data-end="2958">In Lean/Coq:</p>
<ul data-start="2961" data-end="3112">
<li data-start="2961" data-end="3025">
<p data-start="2963" data-end="3025">A “decision tree” is a <strong data-start="2986" data-end="3024">pattern match over inductive types</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3028" data-end="3112">
<p data-start="3030" data-end="3112">An “if–then–else” in hardware corresponds to <strong data-start="3075" data-end="3096">elimination rules</strong> for a sum type.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3114" data-end="3117">
<h2 data-start="3119" data-end="3171"><strong data-start="3122" data-end="3171">5. Propositional Logic in Coq (Core Encoding)</strong></h2>
<pre class="overflow-visible!" data-start="3172" data-end="3431"><div class="contain-inline-size rounded-2xl relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary"><div class="flex items-center text-token-text-secondary px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans justify-between h-9 bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary select-none rounded-t-2xl">coq</div><div class="sticky top-9"><div class="absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2"><div class="bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none py-1" aria-label="Copy"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-sm"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 15.833 12.4688L15.959 12.3975C16.2466 12.2211 16.4808 11.9682 16.