1057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-coq"><span>(* Conjunction *)
Inductive And (A B : Prop) : Prop :=
| conj : A -&gt; B -&gt; And A B.

(* Disjunction *)
Inductive Or (A B : Prop) : Prop :=
| or_introl : A -&gt; Or A B
| or_intror : B -&gt; Or A B.

(* Implication *)
Definition Imp (A B : Prop) := A -&gt; B.
</span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="3433" data-end="3536">Here, <strong data-start="3439" data-end="3455">constructors</strong> (e.g., <code data-start="3463" data-end="3469">conj</code>, <code data-start="3471" data-end="3482">or_introl</code>) are the “proof rules” that inhabit the propositions.</p>
<hr data-start="3538" data-end="3541">
<h2 data-start="3543" data-end="3590"><strong data-start="3546" data-end="3590">6. Building Category-Theoretic Structure</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="3591" data-end="4027">
<li data-start="3591" data-end="3952">
<p data-start="3593" data-end="3656">In Coq/Lean, once you have Π-types and Σ-types, you can define:</p>
<ul data-start="3659" data-end="3952">
<li data-start="3659" data-end="3723">
<p data-start="3661" data-end="3723"><strong data-start="3661" data-end="3683">Monoidal structure</strong> (tensor = product, unit = <code data-start="3710" data-end="3716">unit</code> type).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3726" data-end="3784">
<p data-start="3728" data-end="3784"><strong data-start="3728" data-end="3758">Cartesian closed structure</strong> (products, exponentials).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3787" data-end="3876">
<p data-start="3789" data-end="3876"><strong data-start="3789" data-end="3800">Functor</strong>: maps between type categories (e.g., <code data-start="3838" data-end="3846">Option</code> as an endofunctor on <code data-start="3868" data-end="3874">Type</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3879" data-end="3952">
<p data-start="3881" data-end="3952"><strong data-start="3881" data-end="3890">Monad</strong>: return + bind (used for sequencing in Lean’s <code data-start="3937" data-end="3941">do</code> notation).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3953" data-end="4027">
<p data-start="3955" data-end="4027">Propositional connectives correspond to categorical limits and colimits.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4029" data-end="4032">
<h2 data-start="4034" data-end="4098"><strong data-start="4037" data-end="4098">7. If we generalize “bottom-up” like NAND-based hardware:</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="4099" data-end="4467">
<li data-start="4099" data-end="4162">
<p data-start="4101" data-end="4162"><strong data-start="4101" data-end="4111">Start:</strong> atomic propositions as <code data-start="4135" data-end="4141">Prop</code> (or <code data-start="4146" data-end="4152">Type</code> in Lean).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4163" data-end="4228">
<p data-start="4165" data-end="4228"><strong data-start="4165" data-end="4175">Build:</strong> connectives (<code data-start="4189" data-end="4194">And</code>, <code data-start="4196" data-end="4200">Or</code>, <code data-start="4202" data-end="4207">Imp</code>) as inductive types.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4229" data-end="4270">
<p data-start="4231" data-end="4270"><strong data-start="4231" data-end="4240">Then:</strong> quantifiers as Π and Σ types.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4271" data-end="4345">
<p data-start="4273" data-end="4345"><strong data-start="4273" data-end="4282">Then:</strong> higher-order logic by allowing propositions over propositions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4346" data-end="4405">
<p data-start="4348" data-end="4405"><strong data-start="4348" data-end="4357">Then:</strong> category of contexts, substitution = morphisms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4406" data-end="4467">
<p data-start="4408" data-end="4467"><strong data-start="4408" data-end="4417">Then:</strong> dependent types → fibrations → higher categories.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4469" data-end="4575">Essentially, this is <strong data-start="4490" data-end="4529">constructing Coq from the ground up</strong>, analogous to building a CPU from NAND gates.</p>
<hr data-start="4577" data-end="4580">
<h3 data-start="4582" data-end="4635">✅ Now, three options for where we take this next:</h3>
<p data-start="4636" data-end="4709"><strong data-start="4636" data-end="4643">(A)</strong> Show <strong data-start="4649" data-end="4706">a full “bottom-up build” of a minimal Coq-like system</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="4710" data-end="4835">
<li data-start="4710" data-end="4740">
<p data-start="4712" data-end="4740">Start with primitive types</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4741" data-end="4774">
<p data-start="4743" data-end="4774">Add products, sums, functions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4775" data-end="4798">
<p data-start="4777" data-end="4798">Add inference rules</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4799" data-end="4835">
<p data-start="4801" data-end="4835">Add dependent types and universes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4837" data-end="4882"><strong data-start="4837" data-end="4844">(B)</strong> Show <strong data-start="4850" data-end="4879">categorical formalization</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="4883" data-end="5009">
<li data-start="4883" data-end="4913">
<p data-start="4885" data-end="4913">How NAND logic maps to CCC</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4914" data-end="4961">
<p data-start="4916" data-end="4961">How inductive types map to initial algebras</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4962" data-end="5009">
<p data-start="4964" data-end="5009">How universes map to Grothendieck fibrations.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5011" data-end="5110"><strong data-start="5011" data-end="5018">(C)</strong> Show <strong data-start="5024" data-end="5047">an explicit analogy</strong>: <em data-start="5049" data-end="5084">“NAND → ΠΣ-calculus → Coq kernel”</em> in a stepwise refinement.</p>
