<li data-start="2304" data-end="2409">
<p data-start="2306" data-end="2409"><strong data-start="2306" data-end="2322">Observation:</strong> hardware multiplexing logic generalizes to <strong data-start="2366" data-end="2408">proof selection / sum-type elimination</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2411" data-end="2414">
<h1 data-start="2416" data-end="2485"><strong data-start="2418" data-end="2485">Stage 3 — From Propositional Logic → Type Theory (Curry–Howard)</strong></h1>
<ul data-start="2486" data-end="2811">
<li data-start="2486" data-end="2545">
<p data-start="2488" data-end="2545"><strong data-start="2488" data-end="2505">Core insight:</strong> propositions = types, proofs = terms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2546" data-end="2717">
<p data-start="2548" data-end="2569"><strong data-start="2548" data-end="2567">Implementation:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2572" data-end="2717">
<li data-start="2572" data-end="2619">
<p data-start="2574" data-end="2619">Conjunction <code data-start="2586" data-end="2593">A ∧ B</code> = product type <code data-start="2609" data-end="2616">A × B</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2622" data-end="2665">
<p data-start="2624" data-end="2665">Disjunction <code data-start="2636" data-end="2643">A ∨ B</code> = sum type <code data-start="2655" data-end="2662">A + B</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2668" data-end="2717">
<p data-start="2670" data-end="2717">Implication <code data-start="2682" data-end="2689">A → B</code> = function type <code data-start="2706" data-end="2714">A -&gt; B</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2718" data-end="2811">
<p data-start="2720" data-end="2811"><strong data-start="2720" data-end="2741">Hardware analogy:</strong> function composition = wiring; product/sum types = buses and muxes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
