<p data-start="2982" data-end="3094"><strong data-start="2982" data-end="2995">Takeaway:</strong> branching and conditional execution in hardware is equivalent to <strong data-start="3061" data-end="3093">constructive proof selection</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="3096" data-end="3099">
<h1 data-start="3101" data-end="3140"><strong data-start="3103" data-end="3140">Stage 4 — Categorical Foundations</strong></h1>
<ul data-start="3141" data-end="3800">
<li data-start="3141" data-end="3233">
<p data-start="3143" data-end="3233"><strong data-start="3143" data-end="3164">Hardware analogy:</strong> repeated patterns (MUX trees, pipelines) → structural composition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3234" data-end="3501">
<p data-start="3236" data-end="3265"><strong data-start="3236" data-end="3263">Category theory analog:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3268" data-end="3501">
<li data-start="3268" data-end="3287">
<p data-start="3270" data-end="3287">Objects = types</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3290" data-end="3324">
<p data-start="3292" data-end="3324">Morphisms = functions / proofs</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3327" data-end="3393">
<p data-start="3329" data-end="3393">Product = <code data-start="3339" data-end="3346">A × B</code>, coproduct = <code data-start="3360" data-end="3367">A + B</code>, exponential = <code data-start="3383" data-end="3391">A -&gt; B</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3396" data-end="3447">
<p data-start="3398" data-end="3447">Functors = type transformers (<code data-start="3428" data-end="3436">Option</code>, <code data-start="3438" data-end="3444">List</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3450" data-end="3501">
<p data-start="3452" data-end="3501">Natural transformations = polymorphic mappings.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3503" data-end="3800">
<p data-start="3505" data-end="3523"><strong data-start="3505" data-end="3521">Progression:</strong></p>
<ol data-start="3526" data-end="3800">
<li data-start="3526" data-end="3569">
<p data-start="3529" data-end="3569">NAND → Boolean functions → logic gates</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3572" data-end="3627">
<p data-start="3575" data-end="3627">Gates → compositional wiring → logical connectives</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3630" data-end="3676">
<p data-start="3633" data-end="3676">Connectives → types → categorical objects</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3679" data-end="3724">
<p data-start="3682" data-end="3724">MUX / pipelines → functors and morphisms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3727" data-end="3800">
<p data-start="3730" data-end="3800">Decision trees → sum-type pattern matching / coproduct decomposition</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3802" data-end="3805">
<h1 data-start="3807" data-end="3852"><strong data-start="3809" data-end="3852">Stage 5 — Dependent Types and Induction</strong></h1>
<ul data-start="3853" data-end="4199">
<li data-start="3853" data-end="3926">
<p data-start="3855" data-end="3926"><strong data-start="3855" data-end="3876">Hardware analogy:</strong> multi-stage pipelines with conditional routing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3927" data-end="4012">
<p data-start="3929" data-end="4012"><strong data-start="3929" data-end="3956">Type-theoretic analogy:</strong> dependent types → proofs that depend on other proofs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4013" data-end="4199">
<p data-start="4015" data-end="4037"><strong data-start="4015" data-end="4035">Core constructs:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="4040" data-end="4199">
<li data-start="4040" data-end="4092">
<p data-start="4042" data-end="4092">Π-types: dependent functions (<code data-start="4072" data-end="4089">forall x:A, B x</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4095" data-end="4143">
<p data-start="4097" data-end="4143">Σ-types: dependent pairs (<code data-start="4123" data-end="4140">exists x:A, B x</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4146" data-end="4199">
<p data-start="4148" data-end="4199">Inductive types: user-defined data / proof trees.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4201" data-end="4256">Example: length-indexed vectors (dependent array type):</p>
