5.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="06a75985-2866-43d3-9d37-f3bcf2920fdc" data-testid="conversation-turn-24" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-sm:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="06a75985-2866-43d3-9d37-f3bcf2920fdc" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="262">Perfect — here’s a <strong data-start="19" data-end="45">concrete mapping table</strong> linking <strong data-start="54" data-end="77">hardware constructs</strong> (NAND gates, multiplexors, pipelines, etc.) to <strong data-start="125" data-end="154">type-theoretic constructs</strong> (Coq/Lean), so you can see how low-level digital logic generalizes all the way to a proof assistant kernel.</p>
<hr data-start="264" data-end="267">
<h1 data-start="269" data-end="311"><strong data-start="271" data-end="311">Hardware → Type-Theory Mapping Table</strong></h1>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_1rjym_13 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="313" data-end="3072" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="313" data-end="441"><tr data-start="313" data-end="441"><th data-start="313" data-end="338" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="315" data-end="337">Hardware Construct</strong></th><th data-start="338" data-end="372" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="340" data-end="371">Functional Role / Semantics</strong></th><th data-start="372" data-end="411" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="374" data-end="410">Type-Theoretic Analog (Coq/Lean)</strong></th><th data-start="411" data-end="441" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="413" data-end="439">Notes / Interpretation</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="570" data-end="3072"><tr data-start="570" data-end="733"><td data-start="570" data-end="582" data-col-size="sm">NAND gate</td><td data-start="582" data-end="615" data-col-size="sm">Primitive universal logic gate</td><td data-start="615" data-end="656" data-col-size="md">Primitive atomic type or logical axiom</td><td data-start="656" data-end="733" data-col-size="md">NAND is universal → Π/Σ + inductives are universal for constructive logic</td></tr><tr data-start="734" data-end="869"><td data-start="734" data-end="745" data-col-size="sm">NOT gate</td><td data-start="745" data-end="767" data-col-size="sm">Inversion of signal</td><td data-start="767" data-end="788" data-col-size="md">Negation: <code data-start="779" data-end="787">A -&gt; ⊥</code></td><td data-start="788" data-end="869" data-col-size="md"><code data-start="790" data-end="808">¬A := A -&gt; False</code> in Coq; produces a function type that yields an empty type</td></tr><tr data-start="870" data-end="980"><td data-start="870" data-end="881" data-col-size="sm">AND gate</td><td data-start="881" data-end="910" data-col-size="sm">Conjunction of two signals</td><td data-start="910" data-end="934" data-col-size="md">Product type: <code data-start="926" data-end="933">A × B</code></td><td data-start="934" data-end="980" data-col-size="md">Proof of <code data-start="945" data-end="952">A ∧ B</code> = pair of proofs <code data-start="970" data-end="978">(a, b)</code></td></tr><tr data-start="981" data-end="1088"><td data-start="981" data-end="991" data-col-size="sm">OR gate</td><td data-start="991" data-end="1015" data-col-size="sm">Inclusive disjunction</td><td data-start="1015" data-end="1035" data-col-size="md">Sum type: <code data-start="1027" data-end="1034">A + B</code></td><td data-start="1035" data-end="1088" data-col-size="md">Proof of <code data-start="1046" data-end="1053">A ∨ B</code> = constructor <code data-start="1068" data-end="1075">inl a</code> or <code data-start="1079" data-end="1086">inr b</code></td></tr><tr data-start="1089" data-end="1241"><td data-start="1089" data-end="1105" data-col-size="sm">XOR / EQ gate</td><td data-start="1105" data-end="1145" data-col-size="sm">Exclusive condition or equality check</td><td data-start="1145" data-end="1201" data-col-size="md">Boolean equality type: <code data-start="1170" data-end="1177">a = b</code> or dependent sum <code data-start="1195" data-end="1200">Σ _</code></td><td data-start="1201" data-end="1241" data-col-size="md">Can be encoded as inductive equality</td></tr><tr data-start="1242" data-end="1409"><td data-start="1242" data-end="1260" data-col-size="sm">2:1 Multiplexor</td><td data-start="1260" data-end="1284" data-col-size="sm">Conditional selection</td><td data-start="1284" data-end="1344" data-col-size="md">Dependent selection / pattern match: <code data-start="1323" data-end="1343">if c then A else B</code></td><td data-start="1344" data-end="1409" data-col-size="md">Maps directly to sum-type elimination or conditional function</td></tr><tr data-start="1410" data-end="1558"><td data-start="1410" data-end="1426" data-col-size="sm">Multi-bit bus</td><td data-start="1426" data-end="1448" data-col-size="sm">Parallel data paths</td><td data-start="1448" data-end="1483" data-col-size="md">Indexed type / vector: <code data-start="1473" data-end="1482">Vec A n</code></td><td data-start="1483" data-end="1558" data-col-size="md">Each “wire” = element of vector; whole bus = dependent type over length</td></tr><tr data-start="1559" data-end="1689"><td data-start="1559" data-end="1578" data-col-size="sm">Multi-bit AND/OR</td><td data-start="1578" data-end="1598" data-col-size="sm">Bitwise operation</td><td data-start="1598" data-end="1642" data-col-size="md">Map function over vector: <code data-start="1626" data-end="1641">map (λ x → …)</code></td><td data-start="1642" data-end="1689" data-col-size="md">Structural recursion across vector elements</td></tr><tr data-start="1690" data-end="1846"><td data-start="1690" data-end="1713" data-col-size="sm">Multi-way MUX (tree)</td><td data-start="1713" data-end="1739" data-col-size="sm">Decision tree selection</td><td data-start="1739" data-end="1796" data-col-size="md">Pattern match over sum types or nested dependent types</td><td data-start="1796" data-end="1846" data-col-size="md">Branching in hardware → case analysis in logic</td></tr><tr data-start="1847" data-end="2013"><td data-start="1847" data-end="1864" data-col-size="sm">Pipeline stage</td><td data-start="1864" data-end="1897" data-col-size="sm">Sequential propagation / state</td><td data-start="1897" data-end="1941" data-col-size="md">Function composition / monadic sequencing</td><td data-start="1941" data-end="2013" data-col-size="md">Registers in hardware ↔ dependent function outputs delayed / chained</td></tr><tr data-start="2014" data-end="2168"><td data-start="2014" data-end="2039" data-col-size="sm">D flip-flop / register</td><td data-start="2039" data-end="2054" data-col-size="sm">State memory</td><td data-start="2054" data-end="2110" data-col-size="md">Dependent pair with “valid” flag: <code data-start="2090" data-end="2109">Σ valid : bool, A</code></td><td data-start="2110" data-end="2168" data-col-size="md">Captures pipeline staging / time-dependent proof steps</td></tr><tr data-start="2169" data-end="2321"><td data-start="2169" data-end="2194" data-col-size="sm">Decision tree (binary)</td><td data-start="2194" data-end="2226" data-col-size="sm">Multi-level conditional logic</td><td data-start="2226" data-end="2270" data-col-size="md">Inductive type with multiple constructors</td><td data-start="2270" data-end="2321" data-col-size="md">Internal node = predicate, leaves = result type</td></tr><tr data-start="2322" data-end="2466"><td data-start="2322" data-end="2345" data-col-size="sm">Comparator (GT / EQ)</td><td data-start="2345" data-end="2366" data-col-size="sm">Evaluate predicate</td><td data-start="2366" data-end="2416" data-col-size="md">Boolean function over types / proof of relation</td><td data-start="2416" data-end="2466" data-col-size="md">Proof of <code data-start="2427" data-end="2434">a &gt; b</code> = inhabitant of type <code data-start="2456" data-end="2464">GT a b</code></td></tr><tr data-start="2467" data-end="2603"><td data-start="2467" data-end="2487" data-col-size="sm">Decoder / one-hot</td><td data-start="2487" data-end="2515" data-col-size="sm">Select exactly one branch</td><td data-start="2515" data-end="2544" data-col-size="md">Dependent sum (<code data-start="2532" data-end="2542">Σ i, P i</code>)</td><td data-start="2544" data-end="2603" data-col-size="md">Hardware selection → one constructor inhabited in logic</td></tr><tr data-start="2604" data-end="2769"><td data-start="2604" data-end="2627" data-col-size="sm">Multi-stage pipeline</td><td data-start="2627" data-end="2664" data-col-size="sm">Composition of combinational logic</td><td data-start="2664" data-end="2705" data-col-size="md">Function composition + dependent types</td><td data-start="2705" data-end="2769" data-col-size="md">Stage n output feeds stage n+1, respecting type dependencies</td></tr><tr data-start="2770" data-end="2886"><td data-start="2770" data-end="2795" data-col-size="sm">Reusable module / chip</td><td data-start="2795" data-end="2811" data-col-size="sm">Encapsulation</td><td data-start="2811" data-end="2839" data-col-size="md">Parametric type / functor</td><td data-start="2839" data-end="2886" data-col-size="md">Type parameterization (Polymorphic modules)</td></tr><tr data-start="2887" data-end="3072"><td data-start="2887" data-end="2916" data-col-size="sm">Test bench / HDL simulator</td><td data-start="2916" data-end="2945" data-col-size="sm">Verification / correctness</td><td data-start="2945" data-end="2983" data-col-size="md">Kernel type-checker / proof checker</td><td data-start="2983" data-end="3072" data-col-size="md">Ensures logical correctness of constructions, analogous to verifying circuit behavior</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 64.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593