<hr data-start="3074" data-end="3077">
<h2 data-start="3079" data-end="3109"><strong data-start="3082" data-end="3109">Key Analogies Explained</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="3110" data-end="4160">
<li data-start="3110" data-end="3279">
<p data-start="3113" data-end="3168"><strong data-start="3113" data-end="3166">Branching hardware = Sum types / pattern matching</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3172" data-end="3279">
<li data-start="3172" data-end="3235">
<p data-start="3174" data-end="3235">Each <code data-start="3179" data-end="3183">if</code> or MUX choice becomes a <strong data-start="3208" data-end="3232">sum type constructor</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3239" data-end="3279">
<p data-start="3241" data-end="3279">Multi-level trees = nested inductives.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3281" data-end="3418">
<p data-start="3284" data-end="3331"><strong data-start="3284" data-end="3329">Bitwise buses = Indexed / dependent types</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3335" data-end="3418">
<li data-start="3335" data-end="3361">
<p data-start="3337" data-end="3361"><code data-start="3337" data-end="3340">N</code> wires = <code data-start="3349" data-end="3358">Vec A N</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3365" data-end="3418">
<p data-start="3367" data-end="3418">Operations on buses = <code data-start="3389" data-end="3394">map</code> or recursive functions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3420" data-end="3620">
<p data-start="3423" data-end="3500"><strong data-start="3423" data-end="3498">Pipeline / sequential logic = function composition / monadic sequencing</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3504" data-end="3620">
<li data-start="3504" data-end="3571">
<p data-start="3506" data-end="3571">Registers hold state → output of one function feeds next stage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3575" data-end="3620">
<p data-start="3577" data-end="3620"><code data-start="3577" data-end="3584">valid</code> flags ↔ dependent proof conditions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3622" data-end="3738">
<p data-start="3625" data-end="3675"><strong data-start="3625" data-end="3673">Primitive NAND gate = primitive type / axiom</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3679" data-end="3738">
<li data-start="3679" data-end="3738">
<p data-start="3681" data-end="3738">Everything else is composable from a universal primitive.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3740" data-end="3877">
<p data-start="3743" data-end="3808"><strong data-start="3743" data-end="3806">Multi-bit MUX trees = dependent selection over constructors</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3812" data-end="3877">
<li data-start="3812" data-end="3877">
<p data-start="3814" data-end="3877">Hardware selects data word → logic selects proof term / branch.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3879" data-end="4037">
<p data-start="3882" data-end="3927"><strong data-start="3882" data-end="3925">Comparators / predicates = propositions</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3931" data-end="4037">
<li data-start="3931" data-end="3990">
<p data-start="3933" data-end="3990">Evaluates a condition → returns inhabitant of a <code data-start="3981" data-end="3987">Prop</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3994" data-end="4037">
<p data-start="3996" data-end="4037">E.g., <code data-start="4002" data-end="4010">GT a b</code> inhabited only if <code data-start="4029" data-end="4036">a &gt; b</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="4039" data-end="4160">
<p data-start="4042" data-end="4101"><strong data-start="4042" data-end="4099">Hierarchical modules = functors / parameterized types</strong></p>
<ul data-start="4105" data-end="4160">
<li data-start="4105" data-end="4160">
<p data-start="4107" data-end="4160">Encapsulation of logic → parametric, reusable proofs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="4162" data-end="4165">
<p data-start="4167" data-end="4252">This mapping <strong data-start="4180" data-end="4236">lets you see the “bottom-up construction” philosophy</strong> at every stage:</p>
<ul data-start="4254" data-end="4372">
<li data-start="4254" data-end="4372">
<p data-start="4256" data-end="4372">NAND → gates → buses → pipelines → MUX trees → sum/product → dependent types → categorical reasoning → proof kernel.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4374" data-end="4600">It’s essentially the <strong data-start="4395" data-end="4418">same design mindset</strong>, but generalized from circuits to logic: you start with a <strong data-start="4477" data-end="4498">minimal primitive</strong>, define <strong data-start="4507" data-end="4537">composable building blocks</strong>, and systematically <strong data-start="4558" data-end="4599">abstract towards universal constructs</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="4602" data-end="4605">
<p data-start="4607" data-end="4887">If you want, I can <strong data-start="4626" data-end="4689">draw a mini “pipeline diagram” of this analogy in text form</strong> showing <strong data-start="4698" data-end="4781">NAND gates at the bottom → type-level combinators → Coq proof kernel at the top</strong>, fully labeling each mapping. It would be fully textual so you can read and follow it like a schematic.</p>
<p data-start="4889" data-end="4915" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to do that?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6