<h3 data-start="2493" data-end="2515"><strong data-start="2497" data-end="2515">How to read it</strong></h3>
<ol data-start="2516" data-end="2857">
<li data-start="2516" data-end="2605">
<p data-start="2519" data-end="2605"><strong data-start="2519" data-end="2535">Bottom layer</strong> = the primitive (NAND gate) that can generate all Boolean circuits.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2606" data-end="2750">
<p data-start="2609" data-end="2750"><strong data-start="2609" data-end="2626">Middle layers</strong> = abstraction and composition: MUXes, multi-bit buses, pipelines → sum/product → dependent types → categorical structure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2751" data-end="2857">
<p data-start="2754" data-end="2857"><strong data-start="2754" data-end="2767">Top layer</strong> = full Coq/Lean kernel: universe, dependent types, inductive definitions, type checker.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2859" data-end="2972"><strong data-start="2859" data-end="2875">Key insight:</strong> every layer is a <strong data-start="2893" data-end="2931">generalization of the previous one</strong>, keeping the <strong data-start="2945" data-end="2971">same design principles</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2974" data-end="3178">
<li data-start="2974" data-end="3024">
<p data-start="2976" data-end="3024"><strong data-start="2976" data-end="3003">Primitive + composition</strong> → universal system</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3025" data-end="3062">
<p data-start="3027" data-end="3062"><strong data-start="3027" data-end="3060">Branching → pattern selection</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3063" data-end="3103">
<p data-start="3065" data-end="3103"><strong data-start="3065" data-end="3101">Parallelism → dependent indexing</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3104" data-end="3178">
<p data-start="3106" data-end="3178"><strong data-start="3106" data-end="3176">Sequential propagation → function composition / monadic sequencing</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3180" data-end="3183">
<p data-start="3185" data-end="3454">If you like, I can <strong data-start="3204" data-end="3342">also produce a mapping table linking individual HDL gates (NAND, AND, MUX, pipeline) to their exact type-level equivalents in Coq/Lean</strong>, so you could use it as a <strong data-start="3369" data-end="3451">“cheat sheet” when porting hardware design intuition to proof assistant design</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="3456" data-end="3490" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to make that table?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29