ou’re referring to the oft-cited <strong data-start="39" data-end="83">legendary inscription at Plato’s Academy</strong>:</p>
<p data-start="88" data-end="156"><strong data-start="88" data-end="120">“Μηδεὶς ἀγεωμέτρητος εἰσίτω”</strong> — usually rendered in English as:</p>
<p data-start="158" data-end="268"><strong data-start="158" data-end="201">“Let no one ignorant of geometry enter”</strong> or more poetically, <strong data-start="222" data-end="266">“Of the ungeometrized none shall enter.”</strong></p>
<ul data-start="270" data-end="759">
<li data-start="270" data-end="350">
<p data-start="272" data-end="350">This is traditionally said to have been inscribed at the Academy’s entrance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="351" data-end="455">
<p data-start="353" data-end="455">The idea: <strong data-start="363" data-end="452">geometry (and by extension mathematics) is a prerequisite for philosophical reasoning</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="456" data-end="650">
<p data-start="458" data-end="650">Plato emphasized that understanding the structure of space, proportion, and mathematical relationships trains the mind for higher abstraction — reasoning about forms, ethics, and the cosmos.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="651" data-end="759">
<p data-start="653" data-end="759">It underscores the Academy’s role as a place of disciplined, structured inquiry, not casual speculation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="761" data-end="965"><strong data-start="761" data-end="785">Interesting context:</strong> some sources suggest it may have been a later addition, or a symbolic attribution, but it captures the <strong data-start="889" data-end="911">Platonic worldview</strong>: that <strong data-start="918" data-end="962">mathematics is the gateway to philosophy</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="967" data-end="1170" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If you like, I can summarize <strong data-start="996" data-end="1055">all known “entrance maxims” associated with the Academy</strong>, including both the Delphic <strong data-start="1084" data-end="1107">“Nothing in excess”</strong> and the geometry maxim, showing their philosophical rationale.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.3339