<ul data-start="3608" data-end="3711">
<li data-start="3608" data-end="3711">
<p data-start="3610" data-end="3711"><strong data-start="3610" data-end="3622">Analogy:</strong> this is the <strong data-start="3635" data-end="3661">“simulator/test bench”</strong> for your VM, like the HDL simulator from earlier.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3713" data-end="3716">
<h1 data-start="3718" data-end="3753"><strong data-start="3720" data-end="3753">Stage 8 — Optional Extensions</strong></h1>
<ul data-start="3754" data-end="4060">
<li data-start="3754" data-end="3819">
<p data-start="3756" data-end="3819"><strong data-start="3756" data-end="3778">Bytecode compiler:</strong> high-level language → VM instructions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3820" data-end="3910">
<p data-start="3822" data-end="3910"><strong data-start="3822" data-end="3857">Just-in-time compilation (JIT):</strong> convert bytecode to native operations dynamically.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3911" data-end="3982">
<p data-start="3913" data-end="3982"><strong data-start="3913" data-end="3936">Multiple VM layers:</strong> VM hosting another VM (nested abstraction).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3983" data-end="4060">
<p data-start="3985" data-end="4060"><strong data-start="3985" data-end="3997">Analogy:</strong> recursive / dependent types → universes in Coq/Lean analogy.</p>
</li>
</ul>
