<hr data-start="107" data-end="110">
<h2 data-start="112" data-end="147"><strong data-start="115" data-end="147">1. Information Theory &amp; Bits</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="148" data-end="518">
<li data-start="148" data-end="275">
<p data-start="150" data-end="275">Explored the concept of a <strong data-start="176" data-end="183">bit</strong> as the <strong data-start="191" data-end="274">minimum information required to distinguish between two equally likely outcomes</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="276" data-end="385">
<p data-start="278" data-end="385">Discussed <strong data-start="288" data-end="306">generalization</strong>: bits as thresholds or minimal discriminators between states or probabilities.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="386" data-end="518">
<p data-start="388" data-end="518">Multi-bit or entropy-based distinctions handle more than two outcomes, introducing fractional bits in information-theoretic terms.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="520" data-end="523">
<h2 data-start="525" data-end="573"><strong data-start="528" data-end="573">2. Hardware Construction Using NAND Gates</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="574" data-end="906">
<li data-start="574" data-end="672">
<p data-start="576" data-end="672">Introduced the <strong data-start="591" data-end="613">bottom-up approach</strong>: building all logic from a <strong data-start="641" data-end="671">single primitive NAND gate</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="673" data-end="718">
<p data-start="675" data-end="718">Constructed basic gates: NOT, AND, OR, XOR.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="719" data-end="820">
<p data-start="721" data-end="820">Built <strong data-start="727" data-end="746">multi-bit gates</strong> and <strong data-start="751" data-end="775">multiplexors (MUXes)</strong>, including multi-bit and multi-way versions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="821" data-end="906">
<p data-start="823" data-end="906">Showed how to assemble <strong data-start="846" data-end="859">pipelines</strong> and <strong data-start="864" data-end="882">decision trees</strong> using NAND-based logic.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="908" data-end="911">
<h2 data-start="913" data-end="951"><strong data-start="916" data-end="951">3. Boolean Logic → Type Systems</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="952" data-end="1555">
<li data-start="952" data-end="1050">
<p data-start="954" data-end="1050">Transitioned from <strong data-start="972" data-end="990">hardware logic</strong> to <strong data-start="994" data-end="1038">propositional and type-theoretic systems</strong> (Coq/Lean).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1051" data-end="1238">
<p data-start="1053" data-end="1065">Key mapping:</p>
<ul data-start="1068" data-end="1238">
<li data-start="1068" data-end="1099">
<p data-start="1070" data-end="1099">AND → Product types (<code data-start="1091" data-end="1098">A × B</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1102" data-end="1128">
<p data-start="1104" data-end="1128">OR → Sum types (<code data-start="1120" data-end="1127">A + B</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1131" data-end="1171">
<p data-start="1133" data-end="1171">Implication → Function types (<code data-start="1163" data-end="1170">A → B</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1174" data-end="1238">
<p data-start="1176" data-end="1238">Decision trees / MUX → Pattern matching / sum-type elimination</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1239" data-end="1283">
<p data-start="1241" data-end="1283">Multi-bit buses → Indexed types / vectors.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1284" data-end="1340">
<p data-start="1286" data-end="1340">Pipelines → Function composition / monadic sequencing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1341" data-end="1555">
<p data-start="1343" data-end="1386">Established a <strong data-start="1357" data-end="1380">progressive roadmap</strong> from:</p>
<ol data-start="1389" data-end="1555">
<li data-start="1389" data-end="1416">
<p data-start="1392" data-end="1416">NAND → gates → MUX trees</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1419" data-end="1464">
<p data-start="1422" data-end="1464">Propositional logic → Curry–Howard mapping</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1467" data-end="1511">
<p data-start="1470" data-end="1511">Categorical abstraction → dependent types</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1514" data-end="1555">
<p data-start="1517" data-end="1555">Full proof assistant kernel (Coq/Lean)</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1557" data-end="1560">
<h2 data-start="1562" data-end="1605"><strong data-start="1565" data-end="1605">4. Hardware ↔ Type-Theoretic Mapping</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="1606" data-end="2088">
<li data-start="1606" data-end="1948">
<p data-start="1608" data-end="1715">Provided a detailed table mapping <strong data-start="1642" data-end="1674">specific hardware constructs</strong> to their <strong data-start="1684" data-end="1714">type-theoretic equivalents</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1718" data-end="1948">
<li data-start="1718" data-end="1747">
<p data-start="1720" data-end="1747">Registers → dependent pairs</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1750" data-end="1778">
<p data-start="1752" data-end="1778">ALU → function application</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1781" data-end="1826">
<p data-start="1783" data-end="1826">Pipelines → sequential function composition</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1829" data-end="1871">
<p data-start="1831" data-end="1871">Branching → sum types / pattern matching</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1874" data-end="1903">
<p data-start="1876" data-end="1903">MUX → conditional selection</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1906" data-end="1948">
<p data-start="1908" data-end="1948">Test bench → type checker / proof kernel</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1949" data-end="2088">
<p data-start="1951" data-end="2088">Created a <strong data-start="1961" data-end="1993">textual “pipeline schematic”</strong> showing layers from <strong data-start="2014" data-end="2046">NAND gates → Coq/Lean kernel</strong>, emphasizing <strong data-start="2060" data-end="2087">progressive abstraction</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2090" data-end="2093">
<h2 data-start="2095" data-end="2131"><strong data-start="2098" data-end="2131">5. Building a Virtual Machine</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="2132" data-end="2712">
<li data-start="2132" data-end="2642">
<p data-start="2134" data-end="2216">Developed a <strong data-start="2146" data-end="2178">progressive roadmap for a VM</strong> analogous to hardware → type systems:</p>
<ol data-start="2219" data-end="2642">
<li data-start="2219" data-end="2261">
<p data-start="2222" data-end="2261"><strong data-start="2222" data-end="2246">Primitive operations</strong>: bit-level ops</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2264" data-end="2304">
<p data-start="2267" data-end="2304"><strong data-start="2267" data-end="2274">ALU</strong>: arithmetic/logic computation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2307" data-end="2349">
<p data-start="2310" data-end="2349"><strong data-start="2310" data-end="2332">Registers &amp; memory</strong>: multi-bit buses</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2352" data-end="2415">
<p data-start="2355" data-end="2415"><strong data-start="2355" data-end="2393">Instruction Set Architecture (ISA)</strong>: opcodes and operands</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2418" data-end="2476">
<p data-start="2421" data-end="2476"><strong data-start="2421" data-end="2437">Control Unit</strong>: fetch-decode-execute logic, branching</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2479" data-end="2536">
<p data-start="2482" data-end="2536"><strong data-start="2482" data-end="2509">Stack / Program Counter</strong>: function calls, branching</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2539" data-end="2595">
<p data-start="2542" data-end="2595"><strong data-start="2542" data-end="2565">Runtime environment</strong>: execution loop, memory model</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2598" data-end="2642">
<p data-start="2601" data-end="2642"><strong data-start="2601" data-end="2615">Extensions</strong>: compiler, JIT, nested VMs</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li data-start="2643" data-end="2712">
<p data-start="2645" data-end="2712">Emphasized <strong data-start="2656" data-end="2711">analogy to pipelines, MUX trees, and decision trees</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2714" data-end="2717">
<h2 data-start="2719" data-end="2752"><strong data-start="2722" data-end="2752">6. Overall Theme &amp; Insight</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="2753" data-end="3199">
<li data-start="2753" data-end="2919">
<p data-start="2755" data-end="2803">Applied a <strong data-start="2765" data-end="2802">progressive abstraction principle</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2806" data-end="2919">
<li data-start="2806" data-end="2919">
<p data-start="2808" data-end="2919"><strong data-start="2808" data-end="2919">Primitive → Composable → Conditional → Multi-bit / Multi-stage → Abstracted logic → Type system → VM kernel</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2920" data-end="3058">
<p data-start="2922" data-end="3058">Hardware intuition (NAND gates, MUX, pipelines) provides a <strong data-start="2981" data-end="3057">concrete foundation for understanding abstract logic and dependent types</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3059" data-end="3199">
<p data-start="3061" data-end="3199">Branching logic, pipelines, and multi-bit data structures <strong data-start="3119" data-end="3162">directly map to higher-level constructs</strong> in type theory and virtual machines.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3201" data-end="3204">
